WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.334 --> 00:00:18.888
When Jason walked into the gym, Miss Shelly was putting up a sign.

2
00:00:18.889 --> 00:00:22.957
It said: "Donations for Liberty Elementary."

3
00:00:22.958 --> 00:00:27.109
There were empty cardboard boxes lined up beneath the sign.

4
00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:30.324
"What's going on?" he asked.

5
00:00:30.325 --> 00:00:35.013
"An elementary school burned down after last week's lightning storm.

6
00:00:35.014 --> 00:00:39.660
Those kids lost all their books, pencils . . . everything!

7
00:00:39.661 --> 00:00:44.736
Now they need lots of help," Miss Shelly said.

8
00:00:44.737 --> 00:00:49.439
Jason pulled a brand-new eraser out of his pocket.

9
00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:53.678
"Here," he said. "Our first donation."

10
00:00:53.679 --> 00:01:01.401
"Thanks, Jason. That's very sweet," Miss Shelly said.

11
00:01:01.402 --> 00:01:04.893
"Mr. Frick told us about this today," Ethan said.

12
00:01:04.894 --> 00:01:07.783
"I'm going to bring my old calculator tomorrow."

13
00:01:07.784 --> 00:01:12.599
"I'm sure the kids would like any donations," Miss Shelly said.

14
00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:15.874
"But we'll talk more about it later.

15
00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:18.093
Now put on your aprons!

16
00:01:18.094 --> 00:01:27.533
We're making applesauce muffins," Miss Shelly said.

17
00:01:27.534 --> 00:01:30.631
"First we need to mix the dry ingredients.

18
00:01:30.632 --> 00:01:33.962
Bobby, show Ethan how we do it."

19
00:01:33.963 --> 00:01:48.600
"One and a half cups flour," Bobby read from the easel.

20
00:01:48.601 --> 00:01:55.020
"Baking powder and baking soda," Jason continued.

21
00:01:55.021 --> 00:01:58.958
"A half teaspoon of salt," Nina read next.

22
00:01:58.959 --> 00:02:01.612
Everyone looked at Ethan.

23
00:02:01.612 --> 00:02:06.370
"Cinnamon!" he said.

24
00:02:06.371 --> 00:02:12.866
"Great! Now we mix the wet ingredients," Miss Shelly said.

25
00:02:12.867 --> 00:02:18.997
"Melted butter," Izzie said.

26
00:02:18.998 --> 00:02:28.631
"Two-thirds of a cup brown sugar," Bobby said. "Mix well."

27
00:02:28.632 --> 00:02:33.709
"Two eggs," Jason said, cracking an egg.

28
00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:41.201
"One and a half cups applesauce," Ethan read.

29
00:02:41.202 --> 00:02:44.475
"Now we mix the wet and dry together.

30
00:02:44.476 --> 00:02:46.682
But just a little bit.

31
00:02:46.683 --> 00:02:52.265
Too much mixing is not good for muffin batter," Miss Shelly told them.

32
00:02:52.266 --> 00:02:54.976
"I'll pour the wet into the dry bowl.

33
00:02:54.976 --> 00:02:58.341
Ethan, you mix," Izzie said.

34
00:02:58.342 --> 00:03:02.848
"Izzie can be bossy," Bobby said to Ethan.

35
00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:06.800
"But she's nice."

36
00:03:06.801 --> 00:03:10.941
Everyone lined the muffin pan with colorful paper cups.

37
00:03:10.942 --> 00:03:14.629
"Now we pour in the batter," Miss Shelly said.

38
00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:17.334
"But don't fill the cups completely.

39
00:03:17.335 --> 00:03:26.541
The muffins will rise in the oven."

40
00:03:26.542 --> 00:03:30.340
"How long do we bake them for?" Izzie asked.

41
00:03:30.341 --> 00:03:36.904
"Twenty minutes," Miss Shelly said.

42
00:03:36.905 --> 00:03:41.750
Jason was thinking about the kids at Liberty Elementary again.

43
00:03:41.751 --> 00:03:46.792
"Do the Liberty kids have an after-school program?" he asked.

44
00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:48.776
Miss Shelly nodded.

45
00:03:48.777 --> 00:03:53.472
"Their program is meeting in the town hall until the school is fixed."

46
00:03:53.473 --> 00:03:57.744
"Do they need donations too?" Jason asked.

47
00:03:57.745 --> 00:04:02.167
"Yes, they lost most of their craft and cooking supplies.

48
00:04:02.168 --> 00:04:05.897
It will be tough for a while," Miss Shelly said.

49
00:04:05.898 --> 00:04:11.687
"I wish there was something else we could do," Jason thought.

50
00:04:11.688 --> 00:04:13.116
"The muffins are ready!"

51
00:04:13.116 --> 00:04:20.014
Izzie cried, running to the toaster oven.

52
00:04:20.015 --> 00:04:24.567
"After they cool a little, we can try them," Miss Shelly said.

53
00:04:24.568 --> 00:04:28.183
"Wait! Don't eat them!" Jason said suddenly.

54
00:04:28.184 --> 00:04:30.895
"I have an idea!"

55
00:04:30.896 --> 00:04:35.814
"We should give our muffins to Liberty's after-school program!" Jason said.

56
00:04:35.815 --> 00:04:39.957
"We can call them after-school applesauce muffins!"

57
00:04:39.958 --> 00:04:43.159
"Great idea!" Miss Shelly said.

58
00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:46.059
"We can deliver them tomorrow."

59
00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:49.072
"All right!" Jason cheered.

60
00:04:49.073 --> 00:04:56.495
It felt good to help others.

61
00:04:56.496 --> 00:05:14.058
[caption_out@
